<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:39:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How Chinese companies circumvent chips sanctions in Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90902342b82e7a4e1341589437d43338f6d3b73a8451145c61359ae49d2bd102</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:39:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002--ca78b0ef9d25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">High-tech AI chips are hard to get in China because of US restrictions. To get around this, Chinese companies often use offshore computing capacity, particularly in Southeast Asia. The US is also trying to stop it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can Rassvet, 'Russia's Starlink' change the course of the war in Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dc77c6ad1d029e5b1e02308d6b9de547dd179a0405e09e706e81ecdbc81a476</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:39:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T05:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-rassvet-russia-s-starlink-change-the-course-of-the-war-in-ukraine/a-80052579--622ab8b1bc5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-rassvet-russia-s-starlink-change-the-course-of-the-war-in-ukraine/a-80052579?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">SpaceX's US Starlink satellite system has played a key role in countering the Russian military in Ukraine, but now a Russian counterpart is under development. What could this mean for Ukraine in future?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Peter Magyar meets Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Hungary and Ukraine make a fresh start after the icy relations of the Viktor Orban era</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09b265b44742cb3c8ad3948e24d0ec2bcb514a4cf8e87971ee929503ad10b349</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:39:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relation/a-80054175--5597adb6deec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peter-magyar-meets-volodymyr-zelenskyy-hungary-and-ukraine-make-a-fresh-start-after-the-icy-relations-of-the-viktor-orban-era/a-80054175?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of frosty and hostile relations under Hungary's Kremlin-friendly former PM Viktor Orban, his successor, Peter Magyar, and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy seek to reset their countries' ties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40af4db108b6b605271dff8f8ab94167e7908876d3c506bd7a99ab94b58262e5</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Indian nationals are still ending up in Russia's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d469e48ca736ac1ed8265fdcff693230b6afffa23fc91017a935230da5b890f</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537--f2a88cb80a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Whether through deception or desperation, Indians continue to be drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine. What can New Delhi do to protect its citizens from ending up fighting in Ukraine?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Afghanistan, no female doctor often means no treatment for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c2a6bba83f55f455cf5e3cb068f3b8aa83109be4d5de6ae806df2f441f482b1</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053--cac71a2a15bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions of women in Afghanistan, particularly pregnant women, are suffering under Taliban restrictions and are increasingly losing access to life-saving medical care.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Deepfakes and 'US abandons Taiwan' claims spread ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dca7a28323a79f094d5b890e19a58292a0e4b5475acf751f8df0fa5c5a48d108</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834--56b12ab42141.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of local elections, Taiwan is seeing a surge in AI-generated attacks on mayoral candidate Puma Shen, alongside disinformation portraying the US as abandoning the island.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b44d88a98f5054ea447dda7561de4e528794d32bcd39f3664015070e1ac48f0a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: Why do some EU member states use their vetoes to block the accession of certain candidate countries?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ce72c39c1e1a1f51abde0f37c3b459e069538f658956231c2ecdf49166b3e1e</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candi/a-80034401--27cd622204d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candidate-countries/a-80034401?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Individual EU member states use their veto powers to block candidate countries in the accession process — often for reasons of domestic politics. DW takes a look at some cases and examines what's behind them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Iran's medicine supply chain is failing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d3f615eea6d15344f5e116a9881198517f29ea70ed8466323b87285a8d6c2b6</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-iran-s-medicine-supply-chain-is-failing/a-80035268--b9206162e8f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-iran-s-medicine-supply-chain-is-failing/a-80035268?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pharmacies in Iran are closing, hospital deliveries have stalled and patients are rationing doses or turning to black markets.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is North Korea holding back on sending Russia more troops?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b20e81a885b0a535b8f368220088a891d082a557fca77c114ec13a864a85ccb4</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025--db490ffc00f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A North Korean troop buildup Ukraine warned about months ago has yet to materialize, even as strategic cooperation continues. Analysts say Pyongyang is balancing its ties with Moscow and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How cautious investors are struggling to avoid the AI bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3675e7e3f0207fb11d4466dbcd5ac814dab48129526e1916c189d475d275d39</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412--863307befc9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Nvidia to Coreweave, AI and tech stocks have swung sharply in recent months. Some investors still see plenty of room to run, while others are trying to diversify — and finding it harder than expected.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
